"Let $E$ be a finite set of size $m$, let $\\omega$ be a weight function, and let $Z(\\omega;\\mathbf y)$ be its partition function. Define the symmetrized weight and partition function by\n\n$$\n\\widetilde Z(\\omega;\\mathbf y)=\\frac1{m!}\\sum_{\\sigma\\in\\mathfrak S_m}Z(\\omega;\\mathbf y_\\sigma).\n$$\n\n**Symmetrization conjecture.** If $Z(\\omega;\\mathbf y)$ is Rayleigh, then $\\widetilde Z(\\omega;\\mathbf y)$ is Rayleigh. This is stated as an equivalent form of the Big Conjecture and remains open."